# Secrets. Every value this project needs lives in Vercel environment
# variables, never in the repo. A .env file here is a local convenience only and
# must never be committed: it would hold AIRTABLE_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# ABLY_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD and the SendGrid key in one file, in public history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies. package.json + package-lock.json are the record; the tree is not.
node_modules/

# Vercel CLI working directory — contains the linked project and org ids.
.vercel/

# Local noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.idea/
.vscode/
coverage/
